{"Title":"An Act related to the enhancement of public safety to children in the vicinity of an attractive nuisance, a motor vehicle with the purpose of selling frozen desserts","BillNumber":"H3320","DocketNumber":"HD1349","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"CMG1","Name":"Colleen M. Garry","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/CMG1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-10T15:02:03.403"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"CMG1","Name":"Colleen M. Garry","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/CMG1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-10T15:02:03.4033333"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/H3320/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"By Representative Garry of Dracut, a petition (accompanied by bill, House, No. 3320) of Colleen M. Garry relative to warning light violations committed by operators of motor vehicles selling frozen desserts.  Transportation.","DocumentText":"\tSECTION 1. Chapter 101 section 16A of the General Laws is hereby amended by inserting the following new section:\r\n\tSection 2. If a motor vehicle is stopped on a road for the purpose of selling frozen desserts without a functioning and operating amber dome light, or front and rear warning lights, said vehicle shall be subject to a citation and fine of one hundred dollars to be issued by any law enforcement officer. \r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Accompanied","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J27","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J27"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}